---
import HeroBenchmark from "../components/HeroBenchmark.astro";
import ZeroScore from "../components/ZeroScore.astro";
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TwelveWeeks from "../components/TwelveWeeks.astro";
import benchFigure from "../assets/figures/fid-vs-invN.svg";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";

const titleWords = courseMeta.title.split(" ");
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <section class="audit-hero" slot="hero" aria-labelledby="course-title">
    <div class="audit-hero__inner">
      <div class="audit-hero__copy">
        <p class="audit-hero__eyebrow">
          <span>{courseMeta.code}</span>
          <span>{courseMeta.session} / {courseMeta.year}</span>
          <span>Postgraduate</span>
        </p>
        <h1 id="course-title">{titleWords.map((word) => <span>{word}</span>)}</h1>
        <p class="audit-hero__claim">
          FID decides what counts as progress in generative modelling. Change
          the sample size and the score moves; change the network and the
          ranking can reverse. A reported FID is a claim about a protocol, not
          a property of a model.
        </p>
        <a class="audit-hero__action" href="#benchmark">Inspect the benchmark <span aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span></a>
      </div>

      <figure class="audit-hero__visual">
        <HeroBenchmark />
        <div class="audit-hero__ranking">
          <span>Closed-form ranking</span>
          <strong><b data-score="B">B&nbsp; 4.88</b> <i>&lt;</i> <b data-score="A">A&nbsp; 5.12</b></strong>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Reference conditions / d = 2048 / lower is better</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <section class="audit-panel" id="benchmark" aria-labelledby="benchmark-title">
    <header class="audit-panel__header">
      <p>Benchmark 00 / closed-form truth</p>
    </header>
    <div class="audit-panel__intro">
      <h2 id="benchmark-title">A perfect score can miss the shape.</h2>
      <p>
        The candidates you start with never change; the measurement does.
        Each time the measurement is caught out, the bench gains a candidate
        built to show how.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="audit-panel__readout">
      <div>
        <dt><span>R</span> Reference</dt>
        <dd><strong>0.00</strong><small>baseline</small></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><span>A</span> Location shift</dt>
        <dd><strong>5.12</strong><small>true FID</small></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt><span>B</span> Spread shift</dt>
        <dd><strong>4.88</strong><small>true FID</small></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="audit-panel__fault">
        <dt><span>C</span> Shape failure</dt>
        <dd><strong>0.00</strong><small>visibly wrong</small></dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <ZeroScore />
    <p class="audit-panel__verdict">
      <span>Open defect</span>
      A lower number does not guarantee a better distribution.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Postgraduates who have trained or evaluated a generative model at least
    once, and have read a results table without asking what N was. Assumes
    comfort with multivariate Gaussians, matrix decompositions, and Python with
    NumPy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Not for anyone who wants to learn to build generative models; this course
    never trains one. Not for anyone who needs the number to be fine.
  </p>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Build a bench in week 1: a reference distribution and two candidates, small
    enough to run on a laptop and simple enough that every score has a closed
    form. Re-score it every week with that week&rsquo;s method. Reproduce a
    published number and account for the gap. Construct a candidate the score
    gets wrong. Propose a replacement and judge it by the same standard. Keep a
    log.
  </p>

  <h2>What you leave with</h2>
  <p>
    You can read a reported FID and say what it depends on: the number of
    samples, the network that made the features, the reference set and the
    seed. You can estimate how far a score at your N sits above its limit, and
    tell whether the gap between two models is larger than that. You can build
    a distribution the score gets wrong, and write a report that states the
    protocol beside the number. A results table that leaves the protocol out
    will read to you as unfinished, and that change is what the twelve weeks
    are for.
  </p>

  <TwelveWeeks />

  <h2>The bench</h2>
  <p>
    It starts as one reference set and two candidates, in the 2048
    dimensions a feature extractor would have produced, chosen so that every
    score has a closed form and can be checked by hand. It does not stay that
    size. Every candidate after B arrives in the week the score is caught out.
  </p>
  <dl class="bench">
    <dt>R</dt>
    <dd>N(0, I). The reference set.</dd>
    <dt>A</dt>
    <dd>N(0.05&middot;1, I). Mean shifted, covariance untouched. FID 5.12.</dd>
    <dt>B</dt>
    <dd>N(0, 1.1&middot;I). Mean exact, covariance too wide. FID 4.88.</dd>
    <dt>C</dt>
    <dd>
      Week 6. A bimodal mixture with R&rsquo;s mean and R&rsquo;s covariance.
      FID 0, and visibly wrong.
    </dd>
    <dt>D</dt>
    <dd>
      Week 6, and yours. Scores worse than A while looking closer to R, under
      a measure you write down before you look at the number.
    </dd>
    <dt>E</dt>
    <dd>
      Week 8, once the recordings have time in them. Every frame raised by
      the same amount.
    </dd>
    <dt>F</dt>
    <dd>
      Week 8. Every frame kept, their order destroyed. Two instruments
      disagree about whether E or F is the worse candidate.
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <figure class="bench-figure">
    <img
      src={benchFigure.src}
      width={benchFigure.width}
      height={benchFigure.height}
      alt="Estimated FID for candidates A and B plotted against one over N. Every estimate sits far above its true value, and B is measured as further from R than A at every sample size, which reverses the true ordering."
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <figcaption>
      B is closer to R than A is, and no sample size in this sweep says so.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="home-destinations" aria-labelledby="home-destinations-title">
  <h2 id="home-destinations-title">Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>A live bench in week 1, then four lectures. From week 5 each puts an instrument in the page, so you produce the failure before the lecture names it.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>Twelve weeks on one bench, each re-scoring it with that week&rsquo;s method.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>Reproduce a published number in week 5 and break one in week 9. The final report proposes what to print instead, and the measurement log runs under all of it.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Workspace" href="/workspace/">
      <p>Python and a maths lab in the browser, for the experiments the sessions set. Nothing to install.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>The convenor, and the tutor who holds the seed and re-scores the bench every Monday.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Policies" href="/policies/">
      <p>The rules every assessment links to, stated once, and a calculator for planning your grade.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  let cleanupTitle: (() => void) | undefined;
  const initialiseTitle = () => {
  cleanupTitle?.();
  const title = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".audit-hero h1");
  const desktop = window.matchMedia("(min-width: 901px)");

  const fitTitleLines = () => {
    if (!title) return;

    const chamber = title.parentElement;
    if (!chamber) return;
    const chamberStyle = getComputedStyle(chamber);
    const availableWidth =
      chamber.clientWidth -
      parseFloat(chamberStyle.paddingLeft);
    const lines = [...title.querySelectorAll("span")];
    for (const line of lines) {
      line.style.transform = "none";
    }
    if (desktop.matches) {
      const widestLine = Math.max(
        ...lines.map((line) => line.getBoundingClientRect().width),
      );
      const sharedScale = (availableWidth * 0.85) / widestLine;
      for (const line of lines) {
        line.style.transform = `translateX(-0.04em) scaleX(${sharedScale})`;
      }
    }
  };

  if (title) {
    let disposed = false;
    const observer = new ResizeObserver(fitTitleLines);
    observer.observe(title);
    void document.fonts.ready.then(() => { if (!disposed) fitTitleLines(); });
    desktop.addEventListener("change", fitTitleLines);
    cleanupTitle = () => {
      disposed = true;
      observer.disconnect();
      desktop.removeEventListener("change", fitTitleLines);
      cleanupTitle = undefined;
    };
    fitTitleLines();
  }
  };
  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", initialiseTitle);
  document.addEventListener("astro:before-swap", () => cleanupTitle?.());
  initialiseTitle();
</script>

<style>
  .audit-hero {
    grid-column: full;
    color: #f3eee4;
    background: #030305;
    border-block: 1px solid rgb(185 125 28 / 35%);
  }

  .audit-hero__inner {
    display: grid;
    /* Meet the university theme's vertical content rule exactly. The course
       title occupies the margin to its left; the instrument begins at it. */
    grid-template-columns:
      max(
        calc(var(--at-gutter) + var(--at-sidebar-inset)),
        calc((100vw - var(--at-content-inset) - var(--at-content-width)) / 2)
      )
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    height: calc(100svh - var(--at-nav-height));
    min-height: 42rem;
  }

  .audit-hero__copy {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto auto;
    container-type: inline-size;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vh, 2.5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 1.75vw, 2rem);
  }

  .audit-hero__eyebrow,
  .audit-hero__action,
  .audit-hero__visual figcaption,
  .audit-panel__header,
  .audit-panel__readout,
  .audit-panel__verdict span {
    font-family: var(--at-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .audit-hero__eyebrow {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: #c68a2a;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  .audit-hero__eyebrow span + span::before {
    content: "/ ";
    color: rgb(243 238 228 / 35%);
  }

  .audit-hero h1 {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 0;
    min-width: 0;
    contain: inline-size;
    align-self: stretch;
    margin: clamp(0.75rem, 2vh, 1.25rem) 0;
    color: #f3eee4;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 12vw, 4.25rem);
    font-weight: 580;
    line-height: 0.9;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }

  .audit-hero h1 span {
    display: block;
  }

  @media (min-width: 901px) {
    .audit-hero h1 {
      /* The title owns the complete middle row: metadata above, claim below. */
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: space-between;
      font-size: clamp(5.95rem, 11.2vh, 8.9rem);
    }

    .audit-hero h1 span {
      width: max-content;
      white-space: nowrap;
      /* One shared fit preserves the words' relative widths; only the longest
         line terminates at the divider. */
      transform: translateX(-0.04em) scaleX(0.75);
      transform-origin: left center;
    }
  }

  .audit-hero__claim {
    max-width: 35rem;
    margin-block: 0 clamp(1rem, 2.5vh, 1.75rem);
    color: rgb(243 238 228 / 76%);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem);
  }

  .audit-hero__action {
    align-self: flex-start;
    justify-self: start;
    padding-block: 0.7rem;
    color: #c68a2a;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-block-end: 1px solid currentcolor;
  }

  .audit-hero__action:hover {
    color: #e1aa50;
  }

  .audit-hero__visual {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-inline-start: 1px solid rgb(185 125 28 / 25%);
  }

  .audit-hero__visual { padding: 1.5rem 2rem 8rem; }
  .audit-hero__ranking b { font-weight: inherit; }
  .audit-hero__visual[data-active='A'] [data-score='A'],
  .audit-hero__visual[data-active='B'] [data-score='B'] { color: #fff1ce; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .3em; }

  .audit-hero__visual figcaption {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    inset-inline: 2rem;
    inset-block-end: 1.5rem;
    color: rgb(243 238 228 / 50%);
    font-size: 0.67rem;
  }

  .audit-hero__ranking {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    inset-inline-end: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    inset-block-end: clamp(1.5rem, 3vh, 2.5rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    min-width: min(15rem, calc(100% - 3rem));
    padding: 0 0 0.75rem;
    text-align: end;
    color: #f3eee4;
    border-block-end: 1px solid #c68a2a;
  }

  .audit-hero__ranking span,
  .audit-hero__ranking strong {
    font-family: var(--at-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .audit-hero__ranking span {
    color: rgb(243 238 228 / 55%);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .audit-hero__ranking strong {
    color: #c68a2a;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.4rem);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .audit-hero__ranking i {
    padding-inline: 0.5rem;
    color: rgb(243 238 228 / 45%);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .audit-panel {
    margin-block: var(--at-spacing-xl) var(--at-spacing-2xl);
    border: 1px solid var(--at-border);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
  }

  .audit-panel__header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
    color: var(--at-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-xs);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--at-divider);
  }

  .audit-panel__header p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .audit-panel__intro {
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2rem);
  }

  .audit-panel__intro h2 {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .audit-panel__intro p {
    max-width: 39rem;
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  .audit-panel__readout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    margin: 0;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--at-divider);
  }

  .audit-panel__readout > div {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .audit-panel__readout > div + div {
    border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--at-divider);
  }

  .audit-panel__readout dt,
  .audit-panel__readout dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .audit-panel__readout dt {
    color: var(--at-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
  }

  .audit-panel__readout dt span {
    display: block;
    margin-block-end: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--at-primary);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .audit-panel__readout dd {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin-block-start: 1.25rem;
  }

  .audit-panel__readout strong {
    color: var(--at-heading);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .audit-panel__readout small {
    color: var(--at-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
  }

  .audit-panel__fault {
    background: var(--at-warning-soft);
  }

  .audit-panel__verdict {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .audit-panel__verdict span {
    color: var(--at-warning);
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-xs);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .audit-hero__inner {
      height: auto;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .audit-hero__copy {
      min-width: 0;
      grid-template-rows: auto auto auto auto;
      padding-inline: var(--at-gutter);
    }

    .audit-hero__visual {
      min-height: 18rem;
      aspect-ratio: auto;
      border-block-start: 1px solid rgb(185 125 28 / 25%);
      border-inline-start: 0;
    }

    .audit-panel__readout {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .audit-panel__readout > div:nth-child(3) {
      border-inline-start: 0;
    }

    .audit-panel__readout > div:nth-child(n + 3) {
      border-block-start: 1px solid var(--at-divider);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .audit-hero__inner {
      min-height: auto;
    }

    .audit-hero__copy {
      padding-block: 2.5rem;
    }

    .audit-hero__eyebrow span:last-child {
      flex-basis: 100%;
    }

    .audit-hero__eyebrow span:last-child::before {
      content: "";
    }

    .audit-hero__visual {
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 1.5rem .75rem;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      aspect-ratio: auto;
    }
    .audit-hero__visual figcaption {
      position: static;
      text-align: center;
      font-size: .6rem;
    }

    .audit-hero__ranking {
      position: static;
      justify-self: end;
      inset-inline-end: 1rem;
      inset-block-end: 1rem;
      min-width: min(15rem, calc(100% - 2rem));
    }

    .audit-panel__header,
    .audit-panel__verdict {
      align-items: flex-start;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }

  /* The bench: the name in the deck's mono so R, A, B and C read as labels
     rather than as sentences beginning with a capital. */
  .bench {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--at-spacing-sm) var(--at-spacing-md);
    margin-block: var(--at-spacing-lg);
  }

  .bench dt {
    font-family: var(--at-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--at-primary);
  }

  .bench dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .bench-figure {
    margin-inline: 0;
  }

  .bench-figure img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .bench-figure figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--at-spacing-sm);
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
  }

  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
